# Assets

## Ownership Policy

- Shared (used by 2+ apps or by `design_system`) → `packages/app_assets/`
- Application-specific (used by exactly one app) → `apps/<app>/assets/`
- Feature-specific (used by exactly one feature package) → `packages/features/<feature>/assets/`
- Never duplicate the same asset in two locations — if a second consumer appears, promote it to `app_assets`
- `core` owns zero asset knowledge — never add asset files or path constants to `core`

## SVG (Shared)

- Location: `packages/app_assets/assets/svgs/`
- Constants: `AppSvgs` in `packages/app_assets/lib/src/app_svgs.dart`
- Loading: `AppSvgPicture.asset(AppSvgs.iconName)` from `design_system`
- Never `SvgPicture.asset()` directly — breaks package asset loading

## Adding a New SVG

1. Add file to `packages/app_assets/assets/svgs/`
2. Add constant to `AppSvgs`
3. Use `AppSvgPicture.asset(AppSvgs.newIcon)`

## Fonts

- Declared in `packages/design_system/pubspec.yaml` — fonts are part of the Design Language/Typography System, not `app_assets`
- Always via `AppFont` / `AppFontArabic` — never raw family name strings

## Images

- App-specific: `apps/<app>/assets/images/<subfolder>/`
- Shared: `packages/app_assets/assets/images/{illustrations,empty_states,onboarding}/`
- Loading (shared): `Image.asset(path, package: AppAssets.package)` where `AppAssets.package == 'app_assets'`
- Loading (app-owned): `Image.asset(path)` — no `package:` argument

## Lottie / Animations

- Shared: `packages/app_assets/assets/lottie/` and `packages/app_assets/assets/animations/`
- Never store Lottie files in `assets/images/`

## Naming

`snake_case` for all asset files — no spaces or special characters

## Rules

- Declare every asset folder in owning package's `pubspec.yaml` under `flutter.assets`
- PNG assets ≤ 200 KB; provide `@2x` / `@3x` for non-SVG
- Never bundle shared assets in feature packages or `core` — use `app_assets` (shared), the app (app-specific), or the feature package itself (feature-specific)
